cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the paper below."
title: "A Framework for Efficient Search of High-Distance Quantum Stabilizer Codes"
authors:
  - family-names: Karia
    given-names: Utsav
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
type: software
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-05
abstract: >-
  Code, data and results for a unified framework that quantifies how structural
  constraints reduce the search space for quantum stabilizer codes. Includes the
  empirical study of the finite-size correction factors C and C' over 34,775
  published quantum codes, runtime validation on the [[5,1,3]] code, and the
  14-qubit search that produced a [[14,3]] code detecting 91,765 of 91,770
  weight-<=4 errors.
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - stabilizer codes
  - search space reduction
  - semi-perfect quantum codes
  - code tables
